<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes)" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-3> ;
    schema:about "Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Fifth-order (quintic) resolution of the odd-branch hexagon/triangle degeneracy or of the subcritical sigma0 <= 0.25 cases (Bressloff 2001 Section 5), a mean-mode-coupled amplitude equation for the near-resonant K = 0 mode, a Floquet solver or validated reproduction of Rule (2011) Fig. 8 (the vendored fixture is marked diagnostic-only upstream and the script says so), a derivation of the paper's parameter values from first principles, or a comparison with subject drawings of hallucinations",
        "reconstructed_in_script: A paper_scale_tunnel preset (lateral widths / 3.3, q scan to 6): q* = 4.84, lambda_c = 2.60 mm (paper 2.4-3.2), 29 rings fovea to 90 degrees on the alpha = 3/pi map vs 32 on the Horton-Hoyt map (paper 30-36); comparison of the map's magnification with Horton & Hoyt (1991) (RMS 6.8%) and with the 2002 paper's own scale anchors; a Gaussian-only negative control cross-referenced to the vendored registry; and a diagnostic overlay of the Rule (2011) tongue boundaries (16 curves over 5 forcing amplitudes) with its calibration status printed",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Full cubic amplitude coefficients gamma(theta) = [3 s3 Gamma_3 - 2 s2^2 Q]/N with sigmoid derivative weights s2 = (1-2 sigma0)/2, s3 = (6 sigma0(1-sigma0)-1)/6 and the quadratic feedback Q through the resolvent (lambda_c - W_K)^-1 W_K at K = 0 and K = k_i +/- k_j (critical direction removed); eta = 2 s2 Gamma_2 / N with the eta-aware thresholds Lambda_r < Lambda_h; roll stability tested against every perturbation direction theta on a 5-degree grid, squares/rhombi against all external directions; at sigma0 = 1/2 the coefficients reduce to the upstream bare overlaps (gamma(60)/gamma(0) 0.4864 vs 0.4870); a feedback_fraction > 1 flag (near_resonant) and a gamma(0) <= 0 flag (subcritical) mark where the cubic truncation is unreliable; a regime map over A_loc x sigma0 (260 cells) and sweeps over lateral width, lateral inhibition, lateral spread, local inhibition and sigma0",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Gallery of five planforms rendered at each branch's own q* with k_x and k_y quantised to integer torus cycles: derived non-contoured tunnel and spiral (SELECTED: rolls stable with min 2 gamma/gamma0 - 1 = +0.92), contoured cobweb (IMPOSED-unstable), honeycomb (STABLE-coexisting) and the selected rhombic lattice; contoured planforms use the signed envelope with the exact eigenfunction u(phi) and an orientation field drawn as line elements in cortex and, via the tangent map phi_R = phi + theta_R, in the visual field",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Perturbative Fourier-Bessel even/odd dispersion scans with exact parity to the upstream fixture (5 stability_reports, 24 preset runs, all 133 paper-expectation checks counted, 121 pass) kept as branch_selection_upstream; PLUS the exact Hermitian orientation-space operator on e^{2 i m phi}, |m| <= 8, diagonalised directly (top eigenvalue within 3e-4 of the perturbative scan, dq* = 0) whose dominant harmonic derives the contoured/non-contoured regime (switch at local inhibition A_loc ~ 0.24-0.25 where W0 = W1); fixture presets that impose a non-critical harmonic or parity are flagged (imposed_harmonic, parity_imposed_subcritical)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Retinal pullback through the conformal complex-log angular coordinate by default (cortical torus closes exactly: seam 0.00, spiral chirality 0.89 with the LR/UD reflection metric) with the exact 2002 coordinate retained (--retinal-map exact) and its seams quantified on all four half-meridians under full-field, chiral-mirror and bilateral-mirror conventions; retinal morphometrics (ring counts fovea to 90 degrees on the model map and the Horton-Hoyt map, spoke count, cortical roll angle vs visual log-spiral angle)",
        "reported_in_source: Bressloff et al. (2001, 2002): a Euclidean shift-twist symmetric neural field on the orientation-hypercolumn lattice of V1 undergoes a Turing-type instability whose even/odd, contoured (m=1) / non-contoured (m=0) planforms, pulled back through the retino-cortical map (2001 Section 2: x=(alpha/eps)ln(1+eps r/w0), y=beta theta/eps; 2002 Eq. 1.1: y=beta r theta/(w0+eps r)), give Klüver's four form constants; cubic amplitude equations (2001 Eqs. 5.9-5.15) with coefficients built from the firing-rate derivatives sigma_2, sigma_3 and a quadratic-feedback term select rolls, rhombi, squares or hexagons; the 2002 paper states a foveal magnification of 11.5 mm/deg, 30-36 perceived stripes and a cortical wavelength of 2.4-3.2 mm",
        "reported_in_source: Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): cortical rolls map to tunnels, funnels and spirals under the log-polar retino-cortical map (the non-contoured limit)",
        "reported_in_source: Horton & Hoyt (1991): human V1 linear cortical magnification follows M(E) = 17.3/(E + 0.75) mm/deg",
        "reported_in_source: Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011): periodic flicker drives 1:1 (stripe) and 2:1 period-doubling (hexagon) Floquet resonance tongues over forcing period and wave number",
        "reported_in_source: Tamekue, Prandi & Chitour (2024): a Gaussian-only (no Mexican-hat) lateral kernel produces no MacKay-type pattern, used here as the negative control",
        "transfer_boundary: In the contoured (m = 1) regime rolls and squares are unstable for every sigma0 and the cobweb remains an imposed lattice; the non-contoured regime in which tunnels and spirals are SELECTED is reached by lowering the local inhibition to A_loc = 0.15 (a repo-added preset), not by the fixture's parameters",
        "transfer_boundary: Numerical parity to 2.2e-16 is with the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation's stability_reports and runs, not with digitised figures of the 2001 paper; alpha = 3/pi and beta = 1.589/2 are the upstream params.rs values; the parity presets' rendered wavelength 8.7 mm is 3.1x the paper's and the paper-scale preset is a repo-added parameter choice (lateral widths / 3.3) that reaches the paper's wavelength but not the paper's parameter values",
        "transfer_boundary: The conformal angular map removes the pullback seam by construction (the torus closes exactly); the exact 2002 map's seams (left meridian 11.0 full-field; vertical meridians 10.3 chiral-mirror) are quantified, not fixed, because that map cannot close the torus at finite r",
        "transfer_boundary: The quadratic-feedback term is evaluated through the linear resolvent of the same flat-dispersion operator, whose uniform K = 0 mode is nearly marginal; for sigma0 != 1/2 the feedback dominates the bare cubic term (resolvent gain 50-2000) and the script flags these cells near_resonant instead of reporting a selection (178 of 260 regime-map cells are subcritical or feedback-dominated) — a mean-mode-coupled amplitude equation (Matthews & Cox 2000) would be needed there" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/0951-7715/13/4/317>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1137/23M1616686>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability-second-assessor>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity-second-assessor>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation-second-assessor>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-overall-second-assessor>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity-second-assessor>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package-second-assessor>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability-second-assessor>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match-second-assessor> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-10>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-11>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-12>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-13>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-14>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-15>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-16>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-17>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-18>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-19>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v4-bressloff-v1-form-constants-9> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking Neural-Field Bifurcation & Log-Polar Retino-Cortical Geometry" ;
