<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability-second-assessor> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Code-to-model traceability: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every mathematical component in 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py is explicitly cross-referenced in docstrings and comments to equations, sections, and figures of Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) or to exact file and line ranges in the upstream Rust implementation (planform.rs, presets.rs, params.rs), and Section 14 of morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean formalizes the log-polar pullback classification, cubic roll stability criterion, and Floquet period-doubling return map. We deduct 4 points because the codebase maintains two parallel cubic-selection paths (branch_selection_upstream at lines 1082-1210 and branch_selection_full at lines 1219-1370): verify_paper_calibration_parity (line 1998) and verify_paper_calibration_runs (line 2101) test only branch_selection_upstream and perturbative critical_q, whereas all rendering and badges use branch_selection_full and q_mode, which silently diverge on presets such as fig16_odd (q_mode=1.0551 vs critical_q=1.0280), fig29_square_noncontoured (square/cobweb with roll_stable=False vs roll/spiral with roll_stable=True), and fig30_rhombic_noncontoured. We deduct 4 points because Panel A (lines 2933-2952) sets stab_gal = rendered_gallery[0]['stability'] (which in Pass 4 is roll_noncontoured_derived with A_loc=0.15) and plots its invalid n=1 perturbative curve under the label 'Gallery presets even (theta_0=60 deg, xi_hat_lat=1.5, q*=1.49)', misrepresenting the A_loc=1.0 contoured gallery presets (Columns III-V, where q*=1.45). We deduct 3 points because the top-level README.md description (lines 435-458) does not match the current Pass 4 code architecture or CLI flags (--retinal-map, --sigmoid-baseline, chiral-mirror, and repo- added presets)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity-second-assessor> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Model fidelity to source: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script faithfully implements the Bressloff et al. (2001 Section 3-5; 2002 Section 1.1) local orientation harmonics (Eq. 3.12), anisotropic Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling (Eq. 4.9), O(beta^2) perturbative dispersion curves, exact Hermitian orientation-operator diagonalization on |m| <= 8, full cubic amplitude coefficients gamma(theta) = [3*s3*Gamma_3 - 2*s2^2*Q]/N with sigmoid derivatives (s2, s3) and linear resolvent R_K at K = 0 and k_i +- k_j (Eqs. 5.9-5.15), eta-aware hexagon/roll thresholds, and both conformal (2001) and exact two-regime (2002 Eq. 1.1) retino-cortical maps with tangent-map orientation pullback. We deduct 5 points because exact_orientation_modes (lines 855-867) assigns each eigenvector's dominant harmonic via argmax |v_m| on complex exponential components e^{2im*phi} rather than the real harmonic L2 norm sqrt(|v_+m|^2 + |v_-m|^2) = sqrt(2)|v_m| for m >= 1, misclassifying modes with up to 66.7% m=1 power as m=0, shifting the full-operator harmonic flip to A_loc=0.275, and dropping the even_1 curve to NaN at 118/128 wavenumbers at A_loc=0.24. We deduct 5 points because resolvent_apply (lines 926-937) projects out the critical mode only when |lambda_c - lambda_n| < 1e-6*lambda_c, which removes the |k_1 - k_2| = q* triad resonance at theta=60 deg exactly (Q=0.317) but leaves a spurious 1/(lambda_c - lambda(k_-)) double-spike at adjacent grid angles theta=55 deg (Q=0.699) and 65 deg (Q=0.831) whenever s2 != 0, distorting Panel B and shifting the optimal rhombic angle at sigma0=0.4 from 45 deg to 55 deg. We deduct 5 points because quintic saturation/selection terms (2001 Section 5, needed for the odd-branch H0/H_pi degeneracy and sigma0 <= 0.25 subcritical regime), Matthews-Cox (2000) mean-mode-coupled amplitude equations (needed where the nearly marginal K=0 mode makes 178/260 regime-map cells unreliable), and a dynamical solver for Rule et al. (2011) Floquet tongues are not implemented. Finally, we deduct 3 points because cortical and retinal patterns are evaluated as static mode superpositions passed through tanh rather than integrating the V1 neural-field PDE or amplitude ODEs." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation-second-assessor> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script computes a comprehensive suite of morphometrics on its rendered outputs: 2D radial FFT peak k*, harmonic ring power ratios at k/sqrt(3)k/2k, normalized azimuthal excess discriminators (c4 - c2, c6 - c2), retinal chirality, four-meridian excess seam contrast across conformal and exact maps, radial ring counts, azimuthal spoke counts, spiral pitch angles, and RMS relative error (6.8%) against Horton & Hoyt's (1991) human V1 linear cortical magnification law M(E) = 17.3/(E + 0.75) mm/deg over 1-40 deg, plus scale comparisons against Bressloff et al. (2002 Section 1.1). We deduct 6 points because the cubic_coefficients_full CSV export (line 2686) computes 'bare gamma3/N @ same' as 3*s3*v/gamma0 without dividing by N = <u_0^2>, so for all m=1 gallery presets (where N ~ 0.5) the exported bare ratios in bressloff_v1_metrics.csv (lines 38-40: 0.500, 0.416, 0.248...) are half of the actual gamma(theta)/gamma(0) ratios (1.000, 0.832, 0.496...) at sigma0=0.5. We deduct 5 points because the kluver_form_constant CSV rows (line 2643; bressloff_v1_metrics.csv lines 31-32) log the perturbative n=1 critical_q (1.491139) for roll_noncontoured_derived and spiral_noncontoured_derived instead of the rendered m=0 wavenumber q_mode (1.403797) logged in the cubic and retinal_morphometrics rows. We deduct 5 points because the 2.22e-16 parity checks validate the legacy upstream cubic path against another software implementation's fixture (paper-calibration.json, where 12/133 paper checks fail) rather than digitized empirical or published curves, and the Rule (2011) Fig. 8 fixture fails 4/6 acceptance checks (RMS beta error 0.154 vs 0.10 threshold)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-bressloff-v1-form-constants-stability-reports-parity-max>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-critical-branch-parity-flips-over-the-lateral-spread-sweep-0-90>,
