<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-overall-second-assessor> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — MorphoEval overall 85.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Blinded second-assessor pass. The script implements the Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 orientation-hypercolumn model with both the upstream perturbative dispersion/bare-overlap path (reproducing all 5 stability reports and 24 preset runs in paper-calibration.json to 2.22e-16) and an exact orientation-operator diagonalization with full resolvent-coupled cubic amplitude equations (2001 Eqs. 5.9-5.15), seamless conformal complex-log retinal pullbacks, orientation line elements via the tangent map, a paper-scale tunnel preset, 1D/2D parameter sweeps, and Horton & Hoyt (1991) cortical-magnification anchors. However, several concrete mathematical and reporting defects remain in the new full-model path: (1) exact_orientation_modes classifies the dominant harmonic from single complex-exponential components |v_m| rather than the real harmonic norm sqrt(|v_+m|^2 + |v_-m|^2), biasing the m=0 to m=1 transition by sqrt(2) and producing NaNs in the even_1 dispersion curve near A_loc=0.24-0.25; (2) resolvent_apply projects out the critical subspace only at exact equality (|lambda_c - lambda_n| < 1e-6*lambda_c), leaving an unprojected near-resonant 1:2 triad pole at theta=55 deg and 65 deg around theta=60 deg when s2 != 0; (3) the cubic_coefficients_full CSV export omits the 1/N normalization factor in its bare gamma3/N column, halving the reported values for m=1 presets; and (4) parameter-sweep summaries, Panel A's gallery curve, and the top-level README still mix legacy perturbative n=1 numbers or Pass 3 documentation with the Pass 4 exact-operator pipeline. Overall 85.2/100 (faithfulness 82.3, reproducibility 91.9; model-implementation 83.3/100, biological-validation 81.5/100, applicable-only overall 85.2/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 2aac102; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 89, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 2aac102, image/png, 1852599 B, 3577×2495 px, artifact_sha256 59ee2445fa3cc7fe6fa27a91b99eb16d2b412d31933f5869271e80c9a736ef7c (sha256 59ee2445fa3cc7fe6fa27a91b99eb16d2b412d31933f5869271e80c9a736ef7c), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; artifact_sha256: 59ee2445fa3cc7fe6fa27a91b99eb16d2b412d31933f5869271e80c9a736ef7c; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bressloff/driven-neural-fields-registry.json=4f07b5175a48bcb5..., datasets/bressloff/paper-calibration.json=af12b2c1aa3e38fa..., datasets/bressloff/rule-2011-floquet.json=5e349c7b80185de4...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v3. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Bressloff et al. (2001, 2002): a Euclidean shift-twist symmetric neural field on the orientation-hypercolumn lattice of V1 undergoes a Turing-type instability whose even/odd, contoured (m=1) / non-contoured (m=0) planforms, pulled back through the retino-cortical map (2001 Section 2: x=(alpha/eps)ln(1+eps r/w0), y=beta theta/eps; 2002 Eq. 1.1: y=beta r theta/(w0+eps r)), give Klüver's four form constants; cubic amplitude equations (2001 Eqs. 5.9-5.15) with coefficients built from the firing-rate derivatives sigma_2, sigma_3 and a quadratic-feedback term select rolls, rhombi, squares or hexagons; the 2002 paper states a foveal magnification of 11.5 mm/deg, 30-36 perceived stripes and a cortical wavelength of 2.4-3.2 mm | Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): cortical rolls map to tunnels, funnels and spirals under the log-polar retino-cortical map (the non-contoured limit) | Horton & Hoyt (1991): human V1 linear cortical magnification follows M(E) = 17.3/(E + 0.75) mm/deg | Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011): periodic flicker drives 1:1 (stripe) and 2:1 period-doubling (hexagon) Floquet resonance tongues over forcing period and wave number | Tamekue, Prandi & Chitour (2024): a Gaussian-only (no Mexican-hat) lateral kernel produces no MacKay-type pattern, used here as the negative control; reconstructed_in_script: Perturbative Fourier-Bessel even/odd dispersion scans with exact parity to the upstream fixture (5 stability_reports, 24 preset runs, all 133 paper-expectation checks counted, 121 pass) kept as branch_selection_upstream; PLUS the exact Hermitian orientation-space operator on e^{2 i m phi}, |m| <= 8, diagonalised directly (top eigenvalue within 3e-4 of the perturbative scan, dq* = 0) whose dominant harmonic derives the contoured/non-contoured regime (switch at local inhibition A_loc ~ 0.24-0.25 where W0 = W1); fixture presets that impose a non-critical harmonic or parity are flagged (imposed_harmonic, parity_imposed_subcritical) | Full cubic amplitude coefficients gamma(theta) = [3 s3 Gamma_3 - 2 s2^2 Q]/N with sigmoid derivative weights s2 = (1-2 sigma0)/2, s3 = (6 sigma0(1-sigma0)-1)/6 and the quadratic feedback Q through the resolvent (lambda_c - W_K)^-1 W_K at K = 0 and K = k_i +/- k_j (critical direction removed); eta = 2 s2 Gamma_2 / N with the eta-aware thresholds Lambda_r < Lambda_h; roll stability tested against every perturbation direction theta on a 5-degree grid, squares/rhombi against all external directions; at sigma0 = 1/2 the coefficients reduce to the upstream bare overlaps (gamma(60)/gamma(0) 0.4864 vs 0.4870); a feedback_fraction > 1 flag (near_resonant) and a gamma(0) <= 0 flag (subcritical) mark where the cubic truncation is unreliable; a regime map over A_loc x sigma0 (260 cells) and sweeps over lateral width, lateral inhibition, lateral spread, local inhibition and sigma0 | Gallery of five planforms rendered at each branch's own q* with k_x and k_y quantised to integer torus cycles: derived non-contoured tunnel and spiral (SELECTED: rolls stable with min 2 gamma/gamma0 - 1 = +0.92), contoured cobweb (IMPOSED-unstable), honeycomb (STABLE-coexisting) and the selected rhombic lattice; contoured planforms use the signed envelope with the exact eigenfunction u(phi) and an orientation field drawn as line elements in cortex and, via the tangent map phi_R = phi + theta_R, in the visual field | Retinal pullback through the conformal complex-log angular coordinate by default (cortical torus closes exactly: seam 0.00, spiral chirality 0.89 with the LR/UD reflection metric) with the exact 2002 coordinate retained (--retinal-map exact) and its seams quantified on all four half-meridians under full-field, chiral-mirror and bilateral-mirror conventions; retinal morphometrics (ring counts fovea to 90 degrees on the model map and the Horton-Hoyt map, spoke count, cortical roll angle vs visual log-spiral angle) | A paper_scale_tunnel preset (lateral widths / 3.3, q scan to 6): q* = 4.84, lambda_c = 2.60 mm (paper 2.4-3.2), 29 rings fovea to 90 degrees on the alpha = 3/pi map vs 32 on the Horton-Hoyt map (paper 30-36); comparison of the map's magnification with Horton & Hoyt (1991) (RMS 6.8%) and with the 2002 paper's own scale anchors; a Gaussian-only negative control cross-referenced to the vendored registry; and a diagnostic overlay of the Rule (2011) tongue boundaries (16 curves over 5 forcing amplitudes) with its calibration status printed; transfer_boundary: Numerical parity to 2.2e-16 is with the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation's stability_reports and runs, not with digitised figures of the 2001 paper; alpha = 3/pi and beta = 1.589/2 are the upstream params.rs values; the parity presets' rendered wavelength 8.7 mm is 3.1x the paper's and the paper-scale preset is a repo-added parameter choice (lateral widths / 3.3) that reaches the paper's wavelength but not the paper's parameter values | The quadratic-feedback term is evaluated through the linear resolvent of the same flat-dispersion operator, whose uniform K = 0 mode is nearly marginal; for sigma0 != 1/2 the feedback dominates the bare cubic term (resolvent gain 50-2000) and the script flags these cells near_resonant instead of reporting a selection (178 of 260 regime-map cells are subcritical or feedback-dominated) — a mean-mode-coupled amplitude equation (Matthews & Cox 2000) would be needed there | In the contoured (m = 1) regime rolls and squares are unstable for every sigma0 and the cobweb remains an imposed lattice; the non-contoured regime in which tunnels and spirals are SELECTED is reached by lowering the local inhibition to A_loc = 0.15 (a repo-added preset), not by the fixture's parameters | The conformal angular map removes the pullback seam by construction (the torus closes exactly); the exact 2002 map's seams (left meridian 11.0 full-field; vertical meridians 10.3 chiral-mirror) are quantified, not fixed, because that map cannot close the torus at finite r; does_not_claim: Fifth-order (quintic) resolution of the odd-branch hexagon/triangle degeneracy or of the subcritical sigma0 <= 0.25 cases (Bressloff 2001 Section 5), a mean-mode-coupled amplitude equation for the near-resonant K = 0 mode, a Floquet solver or validated reproduction of Rule (2011) Fig. 8 (the vendored fixture is marked diagnostic-only upstream and the script says so), a derivation of the paper's parameter values from first principles, or a comparison with subject drawings of hallucinations." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:2480-2496 — `sweep_summary` (and the `parameter_sweep` CSV rows at `lines 2807-2828` plus `kluver_form_constant` CSV rows at `line 2643`) aggregates `q_star_min`, `q_star_max`, and `parity_flips` from the perturbative `n=1` fields (`critical_q`, `critical_branch`) rather than `critical_q_exact` / `q_mode` and `critical_parity_exact`, causing `bressloff_v1_metrics.csv:55` to report two false parity flips at `A_loc = 0.225, 0.25` and a false `q*_min = 0.729134` from the `O(beta^2)` zero- denominator singularity at `W_1^loc = W_0^loc`, and logging `critical_q = 1.491139` instead of `1.403797` for the `m=0` gallery presets (`bressloff_v1_metrics.csv:31-32,56`).",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:2686 — In the `cubic_coefficients_full` CSV writer, `'bare gamma3/N @ same'` is computed as `3.0 * bs['s3'] * v / bs['gamma0']`, omitting the `1 / N` (`N = <u_0^2>`) factor present in `bs['gamma0']` (`line 992`); for all `m=1` gallery presets (`N ~ 0.5`), the exported bare ratios in `bressloff_v1_metrics.csv:38-40` (`0.500, 0.416, 0.248...`) are halved relative to `gamma(theta)/gamma(0)` (`1.000, 0.832, 0.496...`) at `sigma0 = 0.5`.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:2933-2952 — Panel A defines `stab_gal = rendered_gallery[0]['stability']` (which is `roll_noncontoured_derived` at `A_loc = 0.15`, where `n=1` perturbation theory is invalid because `W_1^loc < W_0^loc`) and plots `stab_gal['even_growth']` (`q* = 1.49`) under the label `'Gallery presets even (theta_0=60 deg, xi_hat_lat=1.5, q*=1.49)'`, misrepresenting the contoured `A_loc = 1.0` gallery presets in Columns III-V (`q* = 1.45`).",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:3361-3390 — `make_gif` passes `envelope_only=True` (`line 3362`) and hardcodes `'non-contoured'` in `fig.suptitle` (`line 3389`) for all five gallery presets, stripping the contoured `argmax_phi` envelope and orientation line elements from Columns 3-5 (`fig31_square_even`, `fig35_hex_zero_even`, `fig33_rhombic_even`) and mislabeling them as non-contoured in `docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif`.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:855 — `exact_orientation_modes` computes the dominant harmonic via `dom = int(abs(_HARM_M[int(np.argmax(np.abs(v)))]))` on complex exponential coefficients `e^{2im*phi}` instead of combining conjugate pairs into the real harmonic L2 norm `sqrt(|v_+m|^2 + |v_-m|^2) = sqrt(2)*|v_m|` for `m >= 1`; this biases the m=0 vs m=1 classification by sqrt(2), misclassifies modes with up to 66.7% m=1 power (e.g. A_loc=0.24-0.25) as `harmonic=0`, shifts the reported full-operator harmonic flip to `A_loc=0.275` (`bressloff_v1_metrics.csv:47`), and leaves `exact_curves['even_1']` as `NaN` at 118/128 wavenumbers at `A_loc=0.24`.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:926-937 — `resolvent_apply` projects out the critical eigenspace only when `abs(lam_c - vals[i]) < 1.0e-6 * max(abs(lam_c), 1e-12)`, which removes the `|k_1 - k_2| = q*` triad resonance at `theta = 60 deg` (`Q(60 deg) = 0.3170`) but leaves an unprojected near-resonant pole on the critical branch at adjacent grid angles `theta = 55 deg` (`Q = 0.6991`) and `theta = 65 deg` (`Q = 0.8307`), creating artificial spikes in Panel B for `sigma0 != 0.5` and shifting `rhombic_theta_optimal_deg` from `45 deg` to `55 deg` at `sigma0 = 0.4` (`2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:3598-3601`).",
        "remediation needed: README.md:435-458 — The top-level `README.md` section `### [2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py]` is stale from Pass 3: it states that tunnel and spiral are badged `IMPOSED: unstable`, that the cubic coefficients are bare overlaps without `sigma0` weights or quadratic feedback, that no swept parameter changes the selected family, that the default pullback has a 7-10x left-meridian seam, and that `--self-test` runs 27 checks in ~12 s, contradicting the Pass 4 code and outputs." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.52e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity-second-assessor> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script exposes eight sweepable parameters via --sweep PARAM[:LO:HI[:N]], executes five 1D parameter sweeps (lateral_wide_sigma, lateral_inhibition, lateral_spread_deg, local_inhibition, sigmoid_baseline), and computes a 20x13 2D regime map over A_loc x sigma0 (Panel G), demonstrating continuous wavenumber control, parity flips, and the m=0 to m=1 harmonic transition across roll, square, hexagonal, and rhombic families. We deduct 5 points because parameter_sweep and sweep_summary (lines 2275-2311, 2480-2496, 2807-2828) summarize q_star_min, q_star_max, and parity_flips from the perturbative n=1 scan (critical_q, critical_branch) rather than the exact operator (critical_q_exact, critical_parity_exact); as a result, the local_inhibition sweep in bressloff_v1_metrics.csv (line 55) reports two spurious parity flips at A_loc=0.225 and 0.25 and a dip to q*=0.7291 caused by the O(beta^2) Rayleigh-Schrodinger zero-denominator singularity at W_1^loc = W_0^loc, whereas the exact operator stays even with q* in [0.919, 1.001]. We deduct 5 points because 178 of 260 cells (68.5%) in the A_loc x sigma0 regime map and 24 of 25 points in the sigmoid_baseline sweep are either near_resonant (dominated by the nearly marginal K=0 uniform mode) or subcritical (gamma(0) <= 0) and must be masked out as unreliable (lines 3231-3266). We deduct 4 points because all three lateral coupling sweeps displayed in Panel F (lines 3055-3107) leave the selected pattern family invariant (rhombic throughout, with rolls and squares never stable) and plot only scalar q* curves without rendering multi-parameter morphological grids." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package-second-assessor> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Reproducibility package: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The repository provides both lower-bound dependencies in requirements.txt and an exact environment lockfile in requirements.lock.txt (Python 3.14.7, numpy==2.5.4, scipy==1.16.3, matplotlib==3.10.7, pillow==12.0.0), and the simulation is purely deterministic with no unseeded stochastic calls. Running 'MPLCONFIGDIR=/tmp/mplcfg_second ./venv/bin/python3 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py --self-test' completes in ~80 s with exit code 0 and passes all 38 self-test assertions, including SHA-256 verification of all four input JSON fixtures and end-to-end figure and CSV generation. We deduct 4 points because main() (lines 3798-3806) applies the CLI flags --hemifield-mode, --sigmoid-baseline, and --retinal-map by mutating the global PAPER_PRESETS dictionary in place, polluting global module state across subsequent calls in the same Python process. We deduct 3 points because the top-level README.md invocation guide (line 442) lists stale CLI choices (--hemifield-mode {full-field,bilateral-mirror} without chiral-mirror, omitting --retinal- map and --sigmoid-baseline) and states that --self-test runs 27 checks in ~12 s rather than 38 checks in ~80 s." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability-second-assessor> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Source and data traceability: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script docstring, datasets/bressloff/README.md, and datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib provide complete bibliographic records with resolvable DOIs and PMIDs for all eight primary and supporting publications (Bressloff et al. 2001, 2002; Ermentrout & Cowan 1979; Rule et al. 2011; Horton & Hoyt 1991; Tamekue et al. 2024; Klüver 1966; Matthews & Cox 2000). All four JSON fixtures in datasets/bressloff/ are SHA-256-pinned in FIXTURE_CHECKSUMS and verified at runtime, with explicit provenance attribution to MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c (derived from karacsm/V1-sim) and per-constant attribution in RETINO_CONSTANT_PROVENANCE separating Drasdo/Bressloff constants (w0, eps) from upstream params.rs constants (alpha, beta). We deduct 4 points because datasets/bressloff/driven-neural-fields-registry.json (lines 80-209) includes six model entries attributed to 'nicks-et-al-2021' and 'bolelli-prandi-2025' that lack DOIs, full bibliographic details, or entries in paper_citations.bib. We deduct 3 points because the top-level README.md section for this script (lines 435-458) was not updated after Pass 4 and misstates the current provenance of the gallery presets, cubic equations, retinal map default, and self-test check count." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match-second-assessor> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphological realism / specimen match: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The five-column gallery in bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png and the animation docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif render visually distinct cortical planforms and retinal pullbacks for Klüver's four form-constant families (I. Tunnel/Rings, II. Spiral/Funnel, III. Cobweb/Square, IV. Honeycomb/Hex) plus the cubic-selected Rhombic lattice (V), with seamless conformal log-polar pullbacks (spiral chirality 0.892, seam 0.000), white tangent-map orientation line elements on contoured panels, and accurate SELECTED / STABLE-coexisting / IMPOSED-unstable badges. We deduct 7 points because in the contoured (m=1) regime the model renders Klüver's cobweb (Column III) as an unstable imposed lattice (2*gamma(90 deg) > gamma(0) for all sigma0) and honeycomb (Column IV) as a subdominant coexisting branch behind rhombic, so only two of Klüver's four form constants (the derived m=0 rolls in Columns I-II) are natively selected by the cubic equations. We deduct 5 points because the five main gallery columns render at q* ~ 1.40-1.45 (lambda_c ~ 8.7-9.0 mm, ~5.8 rings across 1-40 deg and 8.4 rings across 0-90 deg), which is ~3.2x coarser than the 30-36 perceived stripes (2.4-3.2 mm cortical wavelength) stated in Bressloff et al. (2002 Section 1.1), while the paper_scale_tunnel preset is relegated to a small inset in Panel D. We deduct 4 points because make_gif (lines 3359-3395) forces envelope_only=True on all five presets, omitting the orientation argmax and oriented line elements and labeling every GIF frame 'non-contoured' even for the contoured presets fig31_square_even, fig35_hex_zero_even, and fig33_rhombic_even. We deduct 4 points because no direct visual overlay or side-by-side comparison is made against empirical psychophysical subject drawings or digitized source paper curves, and Panel C plots upstream Floquet fixture curves that fail 4 acceptance checks (RMS beta error 0.154 > 0.10)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

